gh issue comment 21 --repo "$REPO" --body "## ✅ Complete — Star Runner 3D (verified on port 3000)

**Summary:** Playable Three.js 3D game. Fly the Sketchfab spaceship (\"Low Poly Spaceship\" by EdwiixGG, CC Attribution, UID \`82f637f65f894ffe948300183ebe904d\`), collect 12 stars in 60s, dodge 8 drifting asteroids. Score/lives/timer HUD, start/win/lose/restart loop, WASD+arrows+touch controls, WebAudio blips, starfield + grid arena. Playable entrypoints: repo-root \`index.html\` and \`project/index.html\` (both load the same game; root wraps \`project/\` assets). App server runs in tmux session \`app-server\` on port 3000 serving the repo root — \`http://127.0.0.1:3000/\` returns 200 and runs the game.

**Public game link:** https://agentsloop.github.io/PlayGround/ (Pages deploy from repo; local: \`python3 -m http.server 3000\` → http://127.0.0.1:3000/)

**Final commit:** https://github.com/$REPO/commit/$SHA

**Deployment / test status:**
- \`node project/test.mjs\` — PASSED (entrypoints, game-loop markers, 801KB GLB present)
- Headless-Chrome browser tests vs port 3000 — PASSED on both \`/\` and \`/project/\`: ship loaded, mode=play after Start, lives=3, zero console/page errors
- GLB note: source uses archived \`KHR_materials_pbrSpecularGlossiness\` with no textures; bundled normalizer refused conversion (non-dielectric specular), so original GLB is used with a palette tint + procedural fallback ship

**Known limitations:** Ship colors are approximated with a tint (not original Sketchfab textures); requires internet for Three.js CDN importmap; no persistent high scores.

